#lang turmeric refined
;; `refined` is a trailing token, and a trailing token after the base dialect
;; is a hard TUR-E0330 -- that is the whole of the `#lang` grammar now.
;;
;; The fixture predates the decommission and is kept because the history is
;; the point: `refined` was a SEMANTIC `#lang` layer, which was never a second
;; enable path -- it WAS its experiment, scoped to one file, so
;; `#lang turmeric refined` was exactly `--enable=refined` here.  That lesson
;; is half of why the axis went: a semantic layer is an alias for `--enable`,
;; and the only other member was a `#`-dispatch that should never have been
;; optional.  See docs/archive/lang-layers-decommission-plan.md.
;;
;; `refined` graduated 2026-08-01 (v0.33.0) and aged out of the layer shim at
;; 0.38.0, which is when this became TUR-E0330; the decommission did not change
;; the outcome, only the reason and the wording.  Refinement checking itself is
;; unaffected and unconditional -- `#refine{...}` needs no layer and never did.
(defn main [] : int
  (println "unreachable -- the #lang line is refused first")
  0)
